# Original file modification times
#
# Git does not store per-file mtimes: on clone every file is stamped with the
# checkout moment. These are the ORIGIN SERVER's Last-Modified values -- when
# RAMSOFT actually wrote each file -- recovered from the Wayback Machine's
# preserved response headers (x-archive-orig-last-modified).
#
# These are NOT capture dates. A capture date says only "this existed by then";
# these say when the file was made. Both are recorded in PROVENANCE.tsv.
#
# Every value here is cross-confirmed by the origin's Apache ETag, whose
# inode-size-mtime triple independently encodes the same mtime and the same
# byte count: all entries agree on both.
#
# Paths are relative to the mirror root -- the directory that contains
# www.ramsoft.bbk.org/ (that is mirror/ in the published repository).
# Format: <ISO-8601 mtime>  <path>
# Restore by running this from the mirror root, with MANIFEST at $M:
#   awk '$1!~/^#/{print $1, $2}' "$M" |
#     while read t p; do touch -d "$t" "$p"; done
#
